   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "כׇּל הַמְּנָחוֹת בָּאוֹת כּוּ׳. שְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה לֶחֶם הַפָּנִים – בְּהֶדְיָא כְּתִיב בֵּיהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that according to the opinion of Rabbi Yehuda, «all of the meal offerings come» as ten loaves or wafers, except for the shewbread and the griddle-cake offering of the High Priest, which come as «twelve» loaves or wafers. The Gemara examines the sources for these exceptions: With regard to «the shewbread, it is written explicitly of it:» “And you shall take fine flour and bake twelve cakes of it” (Leviticus 24:5)."
  }
